16479	{"artifactId":"LLD-b9d5c5c40df5a574-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-b9d5c5c40df5a574-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:46:01.519Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of the Define's five acceptance criteria for Story s2 (ac1 counted size on every path including the agent tools, ac2 different sizes for different areas, ac3 size and counts stated in the answer, ac4 unmeasurable is XL and says so, ac5 stated size kept as a hint) and each item of the HLD's s2 scope is designed, and nothing listed as another Story's is built.","evidence":"DEF.md lines 145-149 give ac1-ac5; HLD.md line 205 lists the s2 scope (two measuring sources, the four places that assume a size, the pass after both classification branches, removal of the picker and of the classifier's size, depth as well as task count, child plans, the seven kinds of scope, complete mode for five relational drivers, four namespace drivers and the file listing, Redis and etcd not determined). The design's sections 2.1-2.17 and the acceptance mapping cover each one. The limit removals (s4), handling in parts (s3) and layouts (s5) are not designed here.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"On the plan tree today a stated size is taken as it is on the hinted branch, otherwise pickScope picks one with a fallback to M, and the classifier returns a required `scope` under a schema that rejects unknown fields.","evidence":"src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:292-323: `if (args.scopeHint !== undefined) { pickedScope = args.scopeHint; ... } else { ... await pickScope({...}) ... } catch { pickedScope = 'M'; ...}`. src/analyze/classifier/schema.ts:45-49: `required: ['target', 'scope', 'focused', 'scopeRef', 'reasoning'], additionalProperties: false`, `scope: { type: 'string', enum: [...] }`.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Four places in the lookup pipeline and the agent tools set M unless a caller stated a size: the one-shot tool, the step tool's start phase, the workflow runner and the free-form lookup; the step tool sends a workspace scope at the repo path.","evidence":"src/mcp/server.ts:1312 `scope: args.scope ?? 'M'`; src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts:51 `const scope = input.scope ?? 'M'` and :58 `scopeRef: { kind: 'workspace', value: repoPath }`; src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:550 `scope: 'M'`; src/analyze/explore/freeform-probe.ts:115 `scope: 'M'`, with :98-103 building a workspace scope with `repoPath: null` when the context has none. The only other literal is the placeholder at orchestrator/driver.ts:667, commented 'The size is not part of either check'.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"resolveTaskScope checks the index for code and docs only, refuses a scope no registered repo contains, does not refuse when the registry is empty or unreadable, and does not accept a generic request.","evidence":"src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts:35 `type TaskFamily = 'code' | 'docs' | 'infra' | 'data'`, :45 `GRAPH_FAMILIES = new Set(['code', 'docs'])`, :73-75. src/analyze/context/invariants.ts:157-184 returns undefined when the registry read fails or `repos.length === 0`; :195-200 throws ScopeNotIndexedError 'no registered repo contains the scope path'; :208-213 throws on zero entities. orchestrator/driver.ts:398 already skips the check for `generic`.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The scope helpers the measure reuses exist with the stated behaviour: inAreaOf keeps the whole repo for a non-module scope at the repo's path and only what lies under a directory otherwise, graphRepoOf, scopeErrorMapping over three error classes, and walkFiles returning `unreadable` and throwing for an unreadable root with a numeric default cap.","evidence":"task-scope.ts:88-107: `if (scope.kind !== 'module' && dir === graphRepoOf(scope)) return () => true; return e => e.file === dir || e.file.startsWith(`${dir}/`)`. invariants.ts:105-111 maps ScopeNotIndexedError, ScopeRefUnresolvedError and ScopeKindTargetMismatchError and returns undefined otherwise. runtimes/infra/_shared.ts:132-175: `cap: number = DEFAULT_FILE_CAP`, `if (dir === root) throw err;`, `unreadable.push(...)`.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The report's `measure` is `unknown` and unfilled today, mergeAnswerReports returns the completeness part and the answer failure only, and completenessHeadLine returns the completeness line when there is a report.","evidence":"src/analyze/completeness.ts:317-333 builds `{ completeness: {...}, ...(answerFailure !== undefined ? { answerFailure } : {}) }` with no measure; :345-351 `if (report !== undefined) return renderCompletenessLine(report);`. HLD.md:107 declares `readonly measure?: RequestMeasure | undefined; // filled by sizing`. No measuring module or RETIRED_ROLE_IDS exists in src today.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"measureDataSource takes 'the pool path and connection id resolveDataScope gives', so the existing function can supply its argument from what the measuring pass holds.","evidence":"resolveDataScope's signature is `(args: TemplateExecuteArgs, templateLabel: string)` and it resolves the scope itself from `args.intent.scopeRef` (lines 39-49). measureResolvedScope holds a ResolvedScope and no TemplateExecuteArgs, so it cannot call it. The mapping it would have to repeat has a rule the design does not state: `poolPath: scope.lookupPath` for a connection, but `poolPath: scope.value` (the scope's OWN path, not the containing repo) for a repo, workspace or manifest directory. The design says only 'the connections registered there'. Also, with no connection id a DataScope names a pool, not one source, and the design does not say how the sum passes each connection to a function typed `(scope: DataScope)`. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/data/_shared.ts]","action":"State how a ResolvedScope becomes a DataScope: either split a pure `dataScopeOf(scope: ResolvedScope): DataScope` out of resolveDataScope and have both use it, or give the rule. State that the sum calls measureDataSource once per id from the pool's list, with `connectionId` set.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Removing `scope` from the classifier's output touches the schema, the prompt file and the validator's checks, and that list is complete.","evidence":"src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts:234-236 builds the user message of every classify call in code: `'Now classify. Emit ONLY the JSON object matching the ClassifiedIntent schema -- no prose, no fenced block. Required fields: target, scope, focused, scopeRef ({kind, value}), reasoning.'`. Left as it is, each call tells the model to emit a field that the schema (additionalProperties false) then rejects. The same file types the call `completeStructured<ClassifiedIntent>` (:155), reads `raw.scope` in a log (:177) and returns `raw`. The validator, which the design names, has no check of the size: every `scope` in validate.ts is `scopeRef` (lines 95-219), and hintedIntentBase passes it a placeholder 'M' (orchestrator/driver.ts:667). [files: src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts, src/analyze/classifier/validate.ts]","action":"Add src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts to 2.13: the 'Required fields' sentence of buildInitialMessages, the type of the structured call, the log line and the return type. Replace 'from the validator's checks' with the validator's parameter type (UnsizedIntent) and the removal of the placeholder at orchestrator/driver.ts:667. Add a test that the user message names no size.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inventory of everything that names the scope picker is complete: its module, prompt, export, role row, boot-validator entry, the driver comment, the two tests that import its classes, the role-list test and the VS Code declaration.","evidence":"A repo-wide search for `scope-picker|pickScope|analyze.scope.pick|ScopePicker` outside docs finds: classifier/scope-picker.ts, classifier/index.ts:28-37, orchestrator/driver.ts:32,299-335, config/role-taxonomy.ts:89, context/boot-validator.ts:120, context/driver.ts:1031 (comment), __tests__/model-schemas-draft-2020.test.ts:24, context/__tests__/model-failure-callers.test.ts:24-27, config/__tests__/role-taxonomy.test.ts:30, vscode-plugin/package.json:712. Each is named in 2.12 or covered by 'the other tests that list prompts or roles'. The remaining hits are unrelated fixture strings. The JetBrains plugin has no literal for the role.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"reportFromLookups has three callers, and the writers of an answer's head are the ones listed in 2.16.","evidence":"Callers: src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1438, src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/bundle.ts:109, src/mcp/analyze-step/answer-turn.ts:36. Head writers: context/bundle.ts:96 (completenessHeadLine), mcp/bundle-md.ts:65 (completenessHeadLine) and :121 (direct), answer-turn.ts:41 (direct), daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:565 (completenessHeadLine) and :591 (direct), orchestrator/driver.ts:566 (`headFinalReport(..., renderCompletenessLine(report))`). No other non-test caller exists.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The per-driver description of the listings is right: sqlite, pg and mysql clamp through clampListLimit; oracle and mssql put the limit in the query text; ClickHouse's listing always throws; the four namespace drivers apply a limit and report `truncated`; the file listing's `limit` is required today.","evidence":"sqlite.ts:224, pg.ts:266, mysql.ts:266 `const cap = clampListLimit(opts?.limit)`; oracle.ts:324 `FETCH FIRST ${cap + 1} ROWS ONLY`; mssql.ts:313 `SELECT TOP ${cap + 1}`; clickhouse.ts:153-154 `async listTables(): Promise<never> { throw new Error('... not yet implemented ...') }`; mongodb.ts:117-130, cassandra.ts:158-171 and dynamodb.ts:169-184 clamp to 1000 and set `truncated`; nats.ts:110-114 computes the limit and discards it (`void limit; truncated: false`), so its complete mode changes nothing. list-files.ts:37 `readonly limit: number`. shared/db-driver.ts:672 and :711 hold the two signatures as quoted, and :520-524 has `truncated` and `supported`.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.5","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A child plan is spawned in one place, the recursive planner, where the depth cap comes from the root's size handed down, and the daemon's plan request takes `rootScope ?? intent.scope` for the depth.","evidence":"src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts:96 `const rootScope = input.rootScope ?? input.intent.scope;`, :121 `const childIntent = extractChildIntent(task);`, :132-139 builds the child input with `rootScope`. The only other caller of runPlanner is src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:452, where :426 reads `const rootScope = parsed.rootScope ?? parsed.intent.scope;`. extractChildIntent requires a string `scope` on the child (:187), which the design keeps as the hint.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A retired per-role setting cannot be named in RETIRED_PATHS, because the reconcile splits a path on every dot while a per-role value is stored under one key that contains dots, and the reconcile keeps keys the catalog does not list.","evidence":"src/config/reconcile.ts:356 `const keys = r.path.split('.');` and its header: 'preserve every un-catalogued key EXCEPT those explicitly on the retired list'. src/config/write-path.ts:10-17: 'Two dynamic-key namespaces use keys that CONTAIN dots ... `models.tasks.<roleId>` ... the reader ... expects the flat key roleTiers[\"context.assemble\"]'. src/config/analyze.ts:360-363 reads `Object.entries(src['tasks'])` and accepts any role key with a valid tier, so a stored value for the removed role would stay until pruned. assertRetiredDisjoint (reconcile.ts:263) compares against catalog paths only, so the extension the design describes is needed.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design keeps sc3 as the HLD sketches it and does not redesign what other Stories own: the scope function and the error mapping (s6), the completeness record (s1), and the caps that s4 removes.","evidence":"HLD.md:123-132 gives the same eight fields as 2.1 (the size is the same five names). The design calls resolveTaskScope, resolveScopeForTarget and scopeErrorMapping unchanged, and adds no error code. walkFiles gains only `null` for 'no cap', with the default at _shared.ts:134 left for s4. The listings keep their limited mode as the default, which the HLD's s2 text asks for (line 205: 'with the limited mode kept for other callers').","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A rejection that is none of the three scope errors can leave the resolution of a symbol or a connection scope, so the measuring pass must catch every rejection and not only the mapped ones.","evidence":"src/analyze/context/scope.ts:196 (`const repos = await deps.listRepos();` in resolveSymbol), :205-207 (findEntitiesByFile, listEntitiesForRepo) and :270 (resolveConnection) have no guard, while the path kinds go through containingRepoOrNull (:167-176), which catches and returns null. invariants.ts:205-207 reads the repo's entities unguarded in the index check. The design's second error case states this and its handling (determined false, XL, a note naming the read).","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1-ac5 maps to at least one named test, and the existing tests the design says it changes exist.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping lists tests for all five criteria of DEF.md:145-149. The tests named as changed exist: src/analyze/__tests__/model-schemas-draft-2020.test.ts:24 and src/analyze/context/__tests__/model-failure-callers.test.ts:24-27 import the picker's classes; src/config/__tests__/role-taxonomy.test.ts:30 lists the role; vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__ holds per-role.test.ts and per-role-engine.test.ts. One gap follows from the change-sites finding: the classifier test asserts the schema only, so it would pass while the user message still asks for a size.","action":"Add the user-message assertion named under change-sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-09T15:46:01.519Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
